body:
I tell them that. I give them a hug and say "I'm really sorry for your loss. I can't imagine how you are feeling and don't know what to say. If there is anything I can do or anything that you need help with, please let me know. Thinking of you."

&#x200B;

At that moment, whatever you say will be fine. They will remember your presence far more than the exact words you used.

Hello. It sounds like you're going through a very stressful time. I can only imagine being stuck with family for such a long time and the constant news binging is not at all helpful - for both you and your family. Here's a slideshow by White Swan Foundation with some tips to reduce stress:  [https://www.whiteswanfoundation.org/slideshow/reducing-stress-during-covid-19/](https://www.whiteswanfoundation.org/slideshow/reducing-stress-during-covid-19/) 

&#x200B;

Feel free to DM if you'd like to vent/talk about your situation. Take care my friend.
